  "result": "Excellent! All 143 tests pass. The payment terms feature is now fully implemented and tested. Here's what was added:\n\n**Changes Made:**\n\n1. **Added TERMS_INVALID error code** in `src/errors.js`\n\n2. **Enhanced `src/dates.js`** with `endOfMonth()` function:\n   - Calculates the last day of a month for any given date\n   - Handles leap years correctly\n   - Returns date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n\n3. **Updated `src/invoices.js`**:\n   - `createInvoice()` now accepts optional `terms` parameter (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n   - Defaults to NET30 if not specified\n   - Calculates `dueDate` based on terms:\n     - NET14: issue date + 14 days\n     - NET30: issue date + 30 days\n     - EOM: last day of the month\n   - Both `terms` and `dueDate` are preserved by `issueInvoice()`, `addLine()`, and `removeLine()`\n   - Added `validateTerms()` helper function\n\n4. **Updated `src/payments.js`**:\n   - `recordPayment()` preserves `terms` and `dueDate` when recording payments\n\n5. **Added comprehensive test suites**:\n   - 4 tests for `endOfMonth()` in `test/dates.test.js`\n   - 18 tests for payment terms in `test/terms.test.js`\n\nThe invoice system now tracks payment deadlines automatically, supporting three common payment term patterns with proper leap year handling and month-boundary arithmetic.",
